{"id": "EUVD-2026-108840", "enisaUuid": "627ef97f-c4d0-3d3b-8be2-74a89a516b20", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nibmveth: h_free logical LAN on open-fail after register\n\nibmveth_open() registers the logical LAN, then allocates the RX\nbuffer pools. A pool failure jumps to out_free_buffer_pools without\nh_free_logical_lan(), so PHYP still owns the buffer-list page when\nit is unmapped. request_irq() failure already issued the hypercall\nbefore taking the same label.\n\nMove that h_free to the shared post-register unwind so both paths\nderegister before the buffer list is unmapped.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:22:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:22:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/decb4d4ead2c71ef698727734ab5024a872eb372", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c54bbdf6f0731102a4bf7f5e4ee535b3ea415996", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a065bd31ec462f6f9c267026b708dd020f122723", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d24fdec1413c656d29298097926e77542785ca0c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af0524bf4ce1a4cbd2946aa81751582951cfcab5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99045"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2a23dc14-cbe5-39c1-95d3-1792c6ffde0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4fbd93b8-fe7c-33e8-a20f-58759438a21b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d43732ce021f4244a4c53a45d57ad0c13c30ed94 <d24fdec1413c656d29298097926e77542785ca0c"}, {"id": "5350d38d-af4f-3b0d-a3bd-d997e96177c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d43732ce021f4244a4c53a45d57ad0c13c30ed94 <a065bd31ec462f6f9c267026b708dd020f122723"}, {"id": "7fbf18fd-2f70-3b12-9f92-d227171b13d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d43732ce021f4244a4c53a45d57ad0c13c30ed94 <decb4d4ead2c71ef698727734ab5024a872eb372"}, {"i